# ============================================================================
# Trained models -- NOT committed on purpose, not an oversight.
#
# models/energy_demand_model.joblib and carbon_emissions_model.joblib are
# 171MB and 174MB respectively (200-tree Random Forests, max_depth=14, on
# ~72K training rows). GitHub HARD-BLOCKS any single file over 100MB from
# being pushed via normal git -- committing these as-is would break `git
# push` outright, not just bloat the repo.
#
# Regenerate them by running notebooks/04_energy_forecasting.ipynb and
# 05_carbon_prediction.ipynb (fully deterministic -- random_state=42
# throughout -- so you'll get byte-for-byte the same model). The much
# smaller anomaly_detection_model.joblib (2.7MB, a single-feature
# Isolation Forest) IS committed, since it's well under any size concern.
#
# If you want the large models version-controlled anyway, use Git LFS
# (`git lfs track "models/*.joblib"`) rather than removing this rule.
# ============================================================================
models/energy_demand_model.joblib
models/carbon_emissions_model.joblib

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

